  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdded a test-only 2D toolpath shape-mask verifier under `crates/motion/tests/common/` and a pure-Rust RGB difference PNG writer with no new dependencies. The helper checks overcut, leftover, progressive rim engagement, symmetry and stock extension. Added helper regressions and generator fixtures for Adaptive and trochoidal paths. Updated the testing instructions and decision record.\n\nRamps contribute only their selected depth interval. Clearance records the deepest actual cutter position covering each cell. A descending helix never clears its entire footprint at its endpoint depth.\n\nThe two radial-engagement fixtures explicitly start with a predrilled 8 mm radius bore at their final floor: Adaptive at `(0, 0, -5)`, trochoidal at `(-20, 0, -6)`. The radius is the 3 mm entry orbit plus the 5 mm cutter radius. Initial stock clearance is bounded by that region and depth. It gives no swept-path coverage credit. The generated paths still must pass their original overcut, leftover, symmetry and stock-extension checks. Engagement bounds are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test shape_masks --test trochoid_slot --test adaptive_hsm`: 11 helper tests passed, 12 trochoidal tests passed, 2 Adaptive tests passed and 5 heavy tests stayed ignored.\n- Adaptive measured maximum cut width: 1.956193 mm against a 2.352 mm limit. Trochoidal: 5.218097 mm against a 5.375 mm limit.\n- Pin: `shape_mask_precleared_bore_respects_its_radius_and_depth` accepts light side cutting with the stated bore, rejects a smaller or shallower bore, rejects overload outside it, and confirms initial stock does not credit generated swept coverage. The existing solid-stock ramp and helix regressions still pass.\n- Isolated mutations: disabling precleared initialization failed the new pin (2.000 mm > 0.688 mm); reverting the Adaptive fixture to solid stock failed its generator pin (10.000 mm > 2.352 mm); reverting the trochoidal fixture failed its generator pin (10.000 mm > 5.375 mm). Each restored pin passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN, 1,033 passed, 0 failed, 53 ignored across 86 motion test binaries (library plus 85 integration suites).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN.\n\nNo runtime CAM code, dependencies, goldens, screenshots or review evidence changed. Difference PNGs are temporary failure artifacts and are not committed. Heavy ignored tests and GUI suites were not run.\n\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: add test-only 2D toolpath shape-mask verifier and RGB diff PNG reporter\nFixes #1768\n",
